(1262329, 158846, 31213, '<td valign="top">One of the rare cases where the sun flare works.  Nice job.</td>', 'One of the rare cases where the sun flare works.  Nice job.', '2005-03-31 18:02:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262331, 160544, 31213, '<td valign="top">I''m sure lots of people are ragging on your goth glow-look.  But I think its still tastefull and pleasant.  Nice job.  Way to think a bit outside the box.</td>', 'I''m sure lots of people are ragging on your goth glow-look.  But I think its still tastefull and pleasant.  Nice job.  Way to think a bit outside the box.', '2005-03-31 18:03:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262335, 159755, 31213, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done.  Good exposure on the stone.....nice sky with eery cloud movement.  Nice work!</td>', 'Very nicely done.  Good exposure on the stone.....nice sky with eery cloud movement.  Nice work!', '2005-03-31 18:05:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262350, 159556, 31213, '<td valign="top">After flipping through lots of images...then hitting this one....these are my thoughts.<br/> <br/>It''s lacking the "special" element.  The "unique" element.  It just has a snapshot-y feel to it.  Its as if you went to a graveyard, whipped out your camera, and just took a simple shot from a normal and uninteresting perspective.  <br/> <br/>The composition is just average.  It''s not visually strong.  Right when someone looks at an image, their eye should be drawn to the focal point.  The way this image is composed, the focal point isn''t imediately evident to the eye.  Is your emphasis on the cross?  <br/> <br/>Now I could be wrong....but it looks like this was taken during the mid afternoon sun....which is not a good time to take pictures because the sun is directly overhead.  What you DO have going (so that your image doesn''t look flat) is the shadows under the trees in the background.  Thats very good.  <br/> <br/>Another problem I have is the lack of imagination that I feel went into this.  When you were entering the challenge, didn''t you think you''d see a lot of images JUST like this one?  You should have the mentality of, "How will my image stand out?  What will make people remember my image?"  It could be with creative low-key lighting, a unique perpective, an uncommon and unconventional technique, or perhaps a very unusual subject.<br/> <br/>Anyways, this is just my 2 cents.  Please take my critiques with a grain of salt.  I''m sure your a great photographer and take pride in your pictures.  I just wanted to give a full detailed critique of you image because it seems like the kind that will finish just in the middle of the pack with few really deep comments that can make your submissions better.  Nothing anoys me more than people who leave pointless comments that don''t benefit the photographer.  <br/> <br/>Happy Shooting!<br/> <br/>Chris A</td>', 'After flipping through lots of images...then hitting this one....these are my thoughts. It''s lacking the "special" element.  The "unique" element.  It just has a snapshot-y feel to it.  Its as if you went to a graveyard, whipped out your camera, and just took a simple shot from a normal and uninteresting perspective.   The composition is just average.  It''s not visually strong.  Right when someone looks at an image, their eye should be drawn to the focal point.  The way this image is composed, the focal point isn''t imediately evident to the eye.  Is your emphasis on the cross?   Now I could be wrong....but it looks like this was taken during the mid afternoon sun....which is not a good time to take pictures because the sun is directly overhead.  What you DO have going (so that your image doesn''t look flat) is the shadows under the trees in the background.  Thats very good.   Another problem I have is the lack of imagination that I feel went into this.  When you were entering the challenge, didn''t you think you''d see a lot of images JUST like this one?  You should have the mentality of, "How will my image stand out?  What will make people remember my image?"  It could be with creative low-key lighting, a unique perpective, an uncommon and unconventional technique, or perhaps a very unusual subject. Anyways, this is just my 2 cents.  Please take my critiques with a grain of salt.  I''m sure your a great photographer and take pride in your pictures.  I just wanted to give a full detailed critique of you image because it seems like the kind that will finish just in the middle of the pack with few really deep comments that can make your submissions better.  Nothing anoys me more than people who leave pointless comments that don''t benefit the photographer.   Happy Shooting! Chris A', '2005-03-31 18:16:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262354, 160333, 31213, '<td valign="top">Love the pic.....I''ll give it a 7.<br/> <br/>I wish that you had either brned and dodged the sky a bit more or boosted the hue/sat and contrast....it would have made a stronger impact in the picture as a whole.  Nice work though.</td>', 'Love the pic.....I''ll give it a 7. I wish that you had either brned and dodged the sky a bit more or boosted the hue/sat and contrast....it would have made a stronger impact in the picture as a whole.  Nice work though.', '2005-03-31 18:19:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262357, 159244, 31213, '<td valign="top">Like the angle.  May have like to see a slightly larger crop...but maybe you had reasons for not showing the bottom (photo debris....etc).  Interesting stones.  Goodluck!</td>', 'Like the angle.  May have like to see a slightly larger crop...but maybe you had reasons for not showing the bottom (photo debris....etc).  Interesting stones.  Goodluck!', '2005-03-31 18:20:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262359, 160462, 31213, '<td valign="top">I would like this a lot more if you ahd cloned out the thing where the walls meet.  What the heck is that?  Looks like a C-stand.</td>', 'I would like this a lot more if you ahd cloned out the thing where the walls meet.  What the heck is that?  Looks like a C-stand.', '2005-03-31 18:21:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262360, 159292, 31213, '<td valign="top">You lucky dog, you!  You totally lucked out this the fog.  I''m sure this will do good.  Wish I had fog.  ARG!  :))<br/> <br/>Goodluck,<br/> <br/>Chris A</td>', 'You lucky dog, you!  You totally lucked out this the fog.  I''m sure this will do good.  Wish I had fog.  ARG!  :)) Goodluck, Chris A', '2005-03-31 18:22:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262363, 160518, 31213, '<td valign="top">Oh man.....you had an awesome situation here.  I''ll give it a good score...but this is what I would have done....<br/> <br/>I would have had someone in a dark black suit standing at the base of the gravestone with the water soaking is pants up to about his shins.  He would be holding a bouque of flowers and wearing a hat from like the 50''s era.  His reflection would have been increadable and the surrealness of the image as a whole would have been out of this world.  Damn!  <br/> <br/>Nice work though.  I understand my idea is a bit crazy and would take a lot of time and energy but I''m a bit crazy too :)<br/> <br/>Goodluck!<br/> <br/>Chris A</td>', 'Oh man.....you had an awesome situation here.  I''ll give it a good score...but this is what I would have done.... I would have had someone in a dark black suit standing at the base of the gravestone with the water soaking is pants up to about his shins.  He would be holding a bouque of flowers and wearing a hat from like the 50''s era.  His reflection would have been increadable and the surrealness of the image as a whole would have been out of this world.  Damn!   Nice work though.  I understand my idea is a bit crazy and would take a lot of time and energy but I''m a bit crazy too :) Goodluck! Chris A', '2005-03-31 18:25:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1262364, 159572, 31213, '<td valign="top">Love the colors! and contrast between the green and blue.</td>', 'Love the colors! and contrast between the green and blue.', '2005-03-31 18:25:50.000000', NULL, 1),
