(1270358, 159003, 8367, '<td valign="top">Very nice tones and idea. IMO, it''s framed a bit too close on the top.<br/>The emotional appeal would be even stronger if the subject was focused on a recent date. Too much burning for a photography contest but presents a nice finished image. <br/>I gave you a 6.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-04 13:53:14.</i></td>', 'Very nice tones and idea. IMO, it''s framed a bit too close on the top.The emotional appeal would be even stronger if the subject was focused on a recent date. Too much burning for a photography contest but presents a nice finished image. I gave you a 6.', '2005-04-04 14:14:45.000000', '2005-04-04 14:53:14.000000', 0),
(1270359, 160261, 3032, '<td valign="top">Puzzled about the score. :( <br/>Expected it above me. ;)<br/> <br/>Interesting subject (with the head of and the caption), reasonably good background, strong composition, pleasing tone.<br/> <br/>Any idea what happend to the head? Did nobody care anymore to put it back on after it fell off? (That was what I was wondering when I saw this photo).<br/></td>', 'Puzzled about the score. :( Expected it above me. ;) Interesting subject (with the head of and the caption), reasonably good background, strong composition, pleasing tone. Any idea what happend to the head? Did nobody care anymore to put it back on after it fell off? (That was what I was wondering when I saw this photo).', '2005-04-04 14:15:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270363, 160554, 6349, '<td valign="top">Hows that fisheye working out for you?  I love fisheyes.  Let me see some other fisheye photos so I can drool over them.</td>', 'Hows that fisheye working out for you?  I love fisheyes.  Let me see some other fisheye photos so I can drool over them.', '2005-04-04 14:20:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270367, 160544, 3032, '<td valign="top">It''s a bit on the soft side (I''m still not sure if it is good or not so good) and the tone a bit dull, but I could definitely see the natural cemetery here. Didn''t deserve this low score, gave it a 6. Keep thinking like this. :)</td>', 'It''s a bit on the soft side (I''m still not sure if it is good or not so good) and the tone a bit dull, but I could definitely see the natural cemetery here. Didn''t deserve this low score, gave it a 6. Keep thinking like this. :)', '2005-04-04 14:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270368, 160033, 31637, '<td valign="top">great placing here and well deserved, this shot is awesome, the DOF, clarity...the comp. Well done on a tough capture.</td>', 'great placing here and well deserved, this shot is awesome, the DOF, clarity...the comp. Well done on a tough capture.', '2005-04-04 14:22:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270373, 160261, 6349, '<td valign="top">yikes, what happened here?  should have done better.  i think images where the subject and the background blend beautifully together but are still visibly distinct don''t do as well as images where the subject pops out obviously on DPC because a lot of people need glasses.  :)</td>', 'yikes, what happened here?  should have done better.  i think images where the subject and the background blend beautifully together but are still visibly distinct don''t do as well as images where the subject pops out obviously on DPC because a lot of people need glasses.  :)', '2005-04-04 14:23:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270380, 160241, 6349, '<td valign="top">One of my favorites of the challenge as well.  Really surprised it didn''t break 6.  Thanks for the write-up too.  I''ve seen things like this at other cemeteries and never knew the story behind it.  I like your view on things.</td>', 'One of my favorites of the challenge as well.  Really surprised it didn''t break 6.  Thanks for the write-up too.  I''ve seen things like this at other cemeteries and never knew the story behind it.  I like your view on things.', '2005-04-04 14:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270385, 160264, 3032, '<td valign="top">I think that loosing some of that sky to include more of the foreground would work a lot better here. Now you have that huge sky part sucking attention away from your actual subject: the cemetery. The sky in a way takes the intimacy of the cemetery away and besides that, it seldomly works to put the horizon in the middle of the frame like that.<br/>Including more of the foreground would look like you are more interested in the cemetery.</td>', 'I think that loosing some of that sky to include more of the foreground would work a lot better here. Now you have that huge sky part sucking attention away from your actual subject: the cemetery. The sky in a way takes the intimacy of the cemetery away and besides that, it seldomly works to put the horizon in the middle of the frame like that.Including more of the foreground would look like you are more interested in the cemetery.', '2005-04-04 14:31:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270406, 160562, 31637, '<td valign="top">now this is a light painting...beautiful, well done.</td>', 'now this is a light painting...beautiful, well done.', '2005-04-04 14:38:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270409, 160351, 11897, '<td valign="top">I thank everyone for the kind comments.<br/>My 2nd challenge shot using raw format,a little experiment using the white balance set on tungsten, just gave it the mood,as Gordon has said.<br/> <br/>Thanks again,<br/>Paul.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-04 14:54:55.</i></td>', 'I thank everyone for the kind comments.My 2nd challenge shot using raw format,a little experiment using the white balance set on tungsten, just gave it the mood,as Gordon has said. Thanks again,Paul.', '2005-04-04 14:39:29.000000', '2005-04-04 15:54:55.000000', 0),
(1270410, 159876, 31637, '<td valign="top">Classic Heida Photography....an instant favorite!</td>', 'Classic Heida Photography....an instant favorite!', '2005-04-04 14:39:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270431, 160012, 31637, '<td valign="top">Hey Wendy! you came so close again to another ribbon, but don''t worry...ribbons are overrated...this image was definatly one of the winners I thought. I was givng you a ten, and then changed it to a seven because Im such a picky voter and didnt see enough texture in the tombstone. In single tombstone photos, I like to see the detail of the stone, but I now realized you went for that High Contrast look and you did the right thing here...this photo rocks! Congrats</td>', 'Hey Wendy! you came so close again to another ribbon, but don''t worry...ribbons are overrated...this image was definatly one of the winners I thought. I was givng you a ten, and then changed it to a seven because Im such a picky voter and didnt see enough texture in the tombstone. In single tombstone photos, I like to see the detail of the stone, but I now realized you went for that High Contrast look and you did the right thing here...this photo rocks! Congrats', '2005-04-04 14:44:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270437, 160071, 31637, '<td valign="top">Great finish here!! nice colors and composition</td>', 'Great finish here!! nice colors and composition', '2005-04-04 14:46:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270447, 160305, 31637, '<td valign="top">Hey Jessica..you did well here again, you are just so consistent with your fabolous images. I like the B and W. I also think this would of looked extra beautiful with a wide angle lens. I congratulate you on a high placement! Keep it up!</td>', 'Hey Jessica..you did well here again, you are just so consistent with your fabolous images. I like the B and W. I also think this would of looked extra beautiful with a wide angle lens. I congratulate you on a high placement! Keep it up!', '2005-04-04 14:49:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270463, 160368, 31637, '<td valign="top">I love the look to this...it dark looking and eery. Great composition</td>', 'I love the look to this...it dark looking and eery. Great composition', '2005-04-04 14:53:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270475, 160597, 31637, '<td valign="top">beautiful composition and the clarity is so good I feel like im there. Listen? wow...I should bring a tape recorder with me next time I go to a cemetary. I love this, the crispness of it, good title...and im so so happy to see you back in the action Kylie...good going!</td>', 'beautiful composition and the clarity is so good I feel like im there. Listen? wow...I should bring a tape recorder with me next time I go to a cemetary. I love this, the crispness of it, good title...and im so so happy to see you back in the action Kylie...good going!', '2005-04-04 14:56:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270494, 160033, 6668, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorites in the challenge as well, I gave it a 10. I agree that it should have finished much higher.</td>', 'This was one of my favorites in the challenge as well, I gave it a 10. I agree that it should have finished much higher.', '2005-04-04 15:07:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270498, 158801, 22537, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon Roberto!  It really was inevitable that you were to get one sooner than later and this photo is simply a validation of your excellent work.  GO FUJI!!</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon Roberto!  It really was inevitable that you were to get one sooner than later and this photo is simply a validation of your excellent work.  GO FUJI!!', '2005-04-04 15:09:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(1270561, 160499, 6532, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments.  I realized the "morning after" the deadline that I had uploaded the wrong file.  I had intended to enter the following image <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=163258" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6532/thumb/163258.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6532/thumb/163258.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6532/thumb/163258.jpg"/></a>.  Notice the absence of "marks in the sky?"  I wonder how I would have done with the correct image....<br/> <br/>The picture was taken with a wide-angle lens and I think a polarizing filter - laying on my back in the middle of the road....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-04 14:51:28.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments.  I realized the "morning after" the deadline that I had uploaded the wrong file.  I had intended to enter the following image .  Notice the absence of "marks in the sky?"  I wonder how I would have done with the correct image.... The picture was taken with a wide-angle lens and I think a polarizing filter - laying on my back in the middle of the road....', '2005-04-04 15:49:42.000000', '2005-04-04 15:51:28.000000', 0),
