(1271766, 158801, 15305, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nfessel:</b></div><hr/><i> this was edited to death. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>All the editing done to the original image is described above. And it would even be valid under Basic Editing.  <br/>To my jugdement, photographic integrity is maintained. My purpose was to enhance textures and contrasts already present in the original image. I didn''t even use sharpen filters or masks of any kind.</td>', 'Originally posted by nfessel: this was edited to death.   All the editing done to the original image is described above. And it would even be valid under Basic Editing.  To my jugdement, photographic integrity is maintained. My purpose was to enhance textures and contrasts already present in the original image. I didn''t even use sharpen filters or masks of any kind.', '2005-04-05 03:39:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1271800, 160261, 17126, '<td valign="top">This, my friend, is an amaaaazing shot.</td>', 'This, my friend, is an amaaaazing shot.', '2005-04-05 04:09:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1271802, 158801, 30807, '<td valign="top">What a delightful image - beautifully lit. I think the post processing has added great impact. For me, I feel that the gravestones would benefit from a bit of contrast and cleaning up, as it seems that we are wallowing in a dirty environment, whereas hopefully we are in a heavenly environment after death. Thinking more deeply, the treatment has successfully contrasted the darkness of this world with the glory of the heavenly, shown by the brightness of the sun. I love the light rays, and would be most interested to see the first image as it was captured. <br/> <br/>I am just buying a new digicam, and wonder if I should have bought one of these, as I am most impressed with the picture. <br/> <br/>Every success to the photographer, who I am sure will go far<br/> <br/>Adrian</td>', 'What a delightful image - beautifully lit. I think the post processing has added great impact. For me, I feel that the gravestones would benefit from a bit of contrast and cleaning up, as it seems that we are wallowing in a dirty environment, whereas hopefully we are in a heavenly environment after death. Thinking more deeply, the treatment has successfully contrasted the darkness of this world with the glory of the heavenly, shown by the brightness of the sun. I love the light rays, and would be most interested to see the first image as it was captured.  I am just buying a new digicam, and wonder if I should have bought one of these, as I am most impressed with the picture.  Every success to the photographer, who I am sure will go far Adrian', '2005-04-05 04:13:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1271821, 160544, 19708, '<td valign="top">Being Artystic® and different may not sit well with voters, but when the power goes off, and you are pleased with your work, then that is all that matters.<br/>Your PP done here set the tone well for the portrayal.<br/></td>', 'Being Artystic® and different may not sit well with voters, but when the power goes off, and you are pleased with your work, then that is all that matters.Your PP done here set the tone well for the portrayal.', '2005-04-05 04:31:33.000000', NULL, 0),
