(1273262, 160335, 32997, '<td valign="top">I love the colours and detail, but find the background busy. Think this shot would look great if you cropped it way down, so that the focus would be on only the first stone-this may just be my artistic preference though..I would cut right down to just above 29 unknown...creating a little more mystery, juxtaposing with the vibrant life of the grass they once bloodied.</td>', 'I love the colours and detail, but find the background busy. Think this shot would look great if you cropped it way down, so that the focus would be on only the first stone-this may just be my artistic preference though..I would cut right down to just above 29 unknown...creating a little more mystery, juxtaposing with the vibrant life of the grass they once bloodied.', '2005-04-06 00:03:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1273641, 158801, 3548, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by davidspyle:</b></div><hr/><i> Told you so!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Balls! . . . Senor . . .<br/>dare I say crystal balls!?   :-)<br/> <br/>How about crystal huevos, then?!  ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by davidspyle: Told you so!!   Balls! . . . Senor . . .dare I say crystal balls!?   :-) How about crystal huevos, then?!  ;-)', '2005-04-06 01:59:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1273687, 160488, 32881, '<td valign="top">Sorry I missed the vote.....super shot! I just love your eye!</td>', 'Sorry I missed the vote.....super shot! I just love your eye!', '2005-04-06 02:18:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(1273851, 160560, 27735, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by charliebaker:</b></div><hr/><i> The angle of this photo points our focus downward rather than upward, causing us to limit our perspective rather than expand our perspective.  I can see in my mind''s eye the rows and rows of white gravemarkers, but they are off the edge of this photo.  Great lighting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I was actually trying to focus the viewer''s attention to the individual gravestone. Based on the score, I probably should have expanded the perspective like you mentioned.</td>', 'Originally posted by charliebaker: The angle of this photo points our focus downward rather than upward, causing us to limit our perspective rather than expand our perspective.  I can see in my mind''s eye the rows and rows of white gravemarkers, but they are off the edge of this photo.  Great lighting.   I was actually trying to focus the viewer''s attention to the individual gravestone. Based on the score, I probably should have expanded the perspective like you mentioned.', '2005-04-06 03:19:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1274833, 160501, 34396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jab119:</b></div><hr/><i> i feel the angle is a little too extream, good idea, but too much angle </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for your comment.  I actually wanted to use an extreme angle in this shot.  I was trying to portray the deceased''s view of the sky.  I liked the image and thought it would do better, but I guess it just didn''t have enough interest to the masses.<br/> <br/>Thanks again!<br/> <br/>2Shay</td>', 'Originally posted by jab119: i feel the angle is a little too extream, good idea, but too much angle   Thank you for your comment.  I actually wanted to use an extreme angle in this shot.  I was trying to portray the deceased''s view of the sky.  I liked the image and thought it would do better, but I guess it just didn''t have enough interest to the masses. Thanks again! 2Shay', '2005-04-06 13:04:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1275121, 159143, 36030, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! it makes me feel mysterious.</td>', 'Congratulations! it makes me feel mysterious.', '2005-04-06 15:22:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(1275140, 158899, 255, '<td valign="top">i love this. definitely one of my favorite shots from this challenge. i was watching the movie ''closer'' the other night, and saw a scene very much like this--but as it was only split second of a shot, i likely would have missed it had i not already seen, and been interested in this photo. <br/> <br/>awesome light and processing...very eerie and very well done!</td>', 'i love this. definitely one of my favorite shots from this challenge. i was watching the movie ''closer'' the other night, and saw a scene very much like this--but as it was only split second of a shot, i likely would have missed it had i not already seen, and been interested in this photo.  awesome light and processing...very eerie and very well done!', '2005-04-06 15:32:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1275156, 159143, 18128, '<td valign="top">WOW!!! wasn`t expecting this !.Learnt such a lot from this site and the many comments.Thankyou ALL.<br/>About the picture .Got to the location with about 10mins of sunlight to go(traffic jam).Had to walk Quite a way to get there too.In all the rush managed to forget my compact flash card in the Car DOH!,But had a spare 64mb in my bag PHEW!.<br/>Anyway could only shoot off 6 pics in raw format but came away with this as one, WOW what a challenge and a ribbon to boot!!!!<br/>THankyou again<br/>(regards to Mr Higgin for the tip on Location !!)</td>', 'WOW!!! wasn`t expecting this !.Learnt such a lot from this site and the many comments.Thankyou ALL.About the picture .Got to the location with about 10mins of sunlight to go(traffic jam).Had to walk Quite a way to get there too.In all the rush managed to forget my compact flash card in the Car DOH!,But had a spare 64mb in my bag PHEW!.Anyway could only shoot off 6 pics in raw format but came away with this as one, WOW what a challenge and a ribbon to boot!!!!THankyou again(regards to Mr Higgin for the tip on Location !!)', '2005-04-06 15:41:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1276804, 160164, 23458, '<td valign="top">Well this was potentially an interesting shot, you know from the comments you have recieved that the main reason it didn''t do well is the size factor. So I wouldn''t worry too much, you obviously have some skill as the great composition of this image demonstrates. <br/> <br/>Good luck next time. Oh, and welcome to the exclusive *ist DS club :).</td>', 'Well this was potentially an interesting shot, you know from the comments you have recieved that the main reason it didn''t do well is the size factor. So I wouldn''t worry too much, you obviously have some skill as the great composition of this image demonstrates.  Good luck next time. Oh, and welcome to the exclusive *ist DS club :).', '2005-04-07 07:33:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1277121, 158801, 15188, '<td valign="top">Although I don''t understand how the clouds could be so much lighter just around the top section of the cross, this is an outstanding photo -- great concept and visual impact.</td>', 'Although I don''t understand how the clouds could be so much lighter just around the top section of the cross, this is an outstanding photo -- great concept and visual impact.', '2005-04-07 11:43:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1277305, 160441, 5112, '<td valign="top">This is a gentle, lovely shot, John.  It somehow manages to bring tears to my eyes, and I have no idea whose grave this is.  I love the little grasses pointing up, the resting broken cross, the grain, the diagonal of the cross being different than that of the base, the shallow DOF.  Excellent work, John.</td>', 'This is a gentle, lovely shot, John.  It somehow manages to bring tears to my eyes, and I have no idea whose grave this is.  I love the little grasses pointing up, the resting broken cross, the grain, the diagonal of the cross being different than that of the base, the shallow DOF.  Excellent work, John.', '2005-04-07 13:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1278225, 160606, 29797, '<td valign="top">I thought this worthy of much higher scores, at least top 5! Very nice shot. The warm tones throughout are very appealing and a nice break from cold dark cemetery shots.</td>', 'I thought this worthy of much higher scores, at least top 5! Very nice shot. The warm tones throughout are very appealing and a nice break from cold dark cemetery shots.', '2005-04-07 22:57:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1278650, 159789, 31865, '<td valign="top">i''m tired of your photographs being so underrated.  this is fantastic.  creative and different.  a unique way to arrive at this effect.</td>', 'i''m tired of your photographs being so underrated.  this is fantastic.  creative and different.  a unique way to arrive at this effect.', '2005-04-08 03:47:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1279020, 160351, 11897, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Beetle:</b></div><hr/><i> I quite like this, but I think it would have helped to give your main subject a touch more "breathing space" on the left. One step back and one to the left might have done achieved that. I like your choice of DOF. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks, the presence of another gravestone to the left would have spoiled the emphasis on the main stone I felt, thanks you would be correct but for this.<br/>Paul.</td>', 'Originally posted by Beetle: I quite like this, but I think it would have helped to give your main subject a touch more "breathing space" on the left. One step back and one to the left might have done achieved that. I like your choice of DOF.   Thanks, the presence of another gravestone to the left would have spoiled the emphasis on the main stone I felt, thanks you would be correct but for this.Paul.', '2005-04-08 10:54:24.000000', NULL, 0),
