(1564872, 160501, 8009, '<td valign="top">Turning the photo upside down would actually be more like the deceased''s POV, but that would probably make it too abstract.<br/>The angle itself works for me, except that it''s difficult to see whether the cross or the trees are the  subject. Might work better if cropped differently, but I can''t "see" an obvious crop to try out.<br/> <br/>My favourite thing about the photo is that everything but the sky looks b/w. It works well here, and  gives the photo a good feel of the kind of serenity you can only find in a cemetary.<br/></td>', 'Turning the photo upside down would actually be more like the deceased''s POV, but that would probably make it too abstract.The angle itself works for me, except that it''s difficult to see whether the cross or the trees are the  subject. Might work better if cropped differently, but I can''t "see" an obvious crop to try out. My favourite thing about the photo is that everything but the sky looks b/w. It works well here, and  gives the photo a good feel of the kind of serenity you can only find in a cemetary.', '2005-07-26 20:08:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1588982, 159229, 41277, '<td valign="top">Good one... i see so many dpc photoes that you capture a gray stormy sky..<br/> <br/>i cant do that.. coz its always clear and sunny here!!!!<br/>arrrrh</td>', 'Good one... i see so many dpc photoes that you capture a gray stormy sky.. i cant do that.. coz its always clear and sunny here!!!!arrrrh', '2005-08-05 15:25:32.000000', NULL, 0),
